WEBVTT

00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.107
This is the orchestrator update,

00:00:15.405 --> 00:00:16.728
to the twenty-fifth of November.

00:00:18.961 --> 00:00:20.710
First, a new look for the portal.

00:00:21.094 --> 00:00:21.794
It is a sample:

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:23.526
a proposal, not yet built.

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:26.129
The functions stay, and the look changes,

00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:29.030
for finance teams and anyone who is not

00:00:29.073 --> 00:00:29.773
a developer.

00:00:30.958 --> 00:00:32.622
The overview opens on three cards:

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.756
green for payments collected,

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:36.718
amber for payments to follow up,

00:00:37.145 --> 00:00:38.382
red for processor errors.

00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:40.613
The numbers add up.

00:00:40.997 --> 00:00:42.831
A payment opens in plain words.

00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:45.690
And routing rules are written as sentences.

00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:48.854
The same page comes four ways:

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:50.646
Statement, Traffic lights,

00:00:51.116 --> 00:00:52.353
Briefing, and Workbook.

00:00:52.865 --> 00:00:54.529
Which look to work in is the open question.

00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:58.525
Now, what changed in the orchestrator.

00:00:58.951 --> 00:00:59.651
Four things:

00:01:00.061 --> 00:01:02.364
an easier payment form, a clearer view of

00:01:02.407 --> 00:01:04.882
every payment, a second admin on Live

00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:07.442
changes, and every merchant in one view.

00:01:09.372 --> 00:01:10.072
Change one:

00:01:10.182 --> 00:01:10.882
the payment form.

00:01:11.206 --> 00:01:12.998
It now takes the shopper's email and

00:01:13.041 --> 00:01:14.620
shipping address from the checkout page,

00:01:15.089 --> 00:01:16.284
so it never asks twice.

00:01:17.785 --> 00:01:18.639
With a shipping address,

00:01:19.065 --> 00:01:20.303
the card shows one box:

00:01:20.772 --> 00:01:22.436
billing address is the same as shipping.

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.953
Tick it, and the billing fields fold away.

00:01:26.346 --> 00:01:28.351
In the portal, each country keeps the

00:01:28.394 --> 00:01:30.186
default fields or sets its own,

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.490
and decides whether that box starts ticked.

00:01:33.258 --> 00:01:35.434
Test and Live each keep their own settings.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.574
With Apple Pay or Google Pay,

00:01:39.001 --> 00:01:40.665
the wallet's own sheet gives the billing

00:01:40.836 --> 00:01:42.841
address, and the email too when the page

00:01:42.926 --> 00:01:43.626
passed none.

00:01:44.775 --> 00:01:46.481
And the form can now be drawn dark,

00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:48.785
and restyled while the shopper is in it,

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.279
without losing what they typed.

00:01:52.989 --> 00:01:53.689
Change two:

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.378
what happened to a payment.

00:01:55.933 --> 00:01:58.280
Type a card's first six or eight digits

00:01:58.408 --> 00:02:00.584
into search, and every payment made with

00:02:00.626 --> 00:02:01.352
that card shows.

00:02:02.854 --> 00:02:04.816
A new filter narrows the list by way

00:02:04.859 --> 00:02:05.559
of paying:

00:02:05.798 --> 00:02:07.888
card, Apple Pay, Google Pay,

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:08.930
or PayPal.

00:02:10.087 --> 00:02:12.519
Open a payment, and each attempt now shows

00:02:12.647 --> 00:02:13.347
three things:

00:02:13.671 --> 00:02:14.780
what we sent the processor,

00:02:15.292 --> 00:02:17.596
what it answered, and our reading in plain words.

00:02:20.062 --> 00:02:21.555
Here, Worldpay declined.

00:02:22.195 --> 00:02:23.816
The payment failed over to Network

00:02:23.859 --> 00:02:25.993
Merchants, and Network Merchants approved it.

00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:28.842
And when a processor's answer is lost,

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:30.762
the payment no longer fails.

00:02:31.488 --> 00:02:33.109
It stays processing while the service

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.114
looks it up, and the shopper is told

00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:36.010
not to pay again.

00:02:37.988 --> 00:02:38.688
Change three:

00:02:38.884 --> 00:02:40.249
a second admin approves.

00:02:41.017 --> 00:02:42.980
In Live mode, a change to how a

00:02:43.022 --> 00:02:45.156
merchant takes payments now waits for more

00:02:45.241 --> 00:02:46.009
than one admin.

00:02:47.257 --> 00:02:49.092
One admin saves a change as a request.

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:51.182
Saving counts as the first approval:

00:02:51.652 --> 00:02:52.462
one of the two it needs.

00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:56.528
The second admin opens Pending changes and approves:

00:02:57.339 --> 00:02:58.064
two of two.

00:02:58.576 --> 00:02:59.771
Only then can it be applied.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:03.427
On our own merchant, six kinds of change

00:03:03.684 --> 00:03:04.665
need two admins.

00:03:05.689 --> 00:03:07.609
Test mode always needs just one,

00:03:07.993 --> 00:03:09.614
so trying things out never waits.

00:03:11.674 --> 00:03:12.374
Change four:

00:03:12.911 --> 00:03:14.063
across every merchant.

00:03:14.618 --> 00:03:16.794
Unicity's own system admins now have a

00:03:16.836 --> 00:03:17.536
Merchants page:

00:03:17.903 --> 00:03:19.396
every merchant and its people,

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:21.231
and where a new merchant is invited.

00:03:22.762 --> 00:03:24.682
A system admin can sign in as one

00:03:24.724 --> 00:03:26.772
of a merchant's admins, under a banner

00:03:26.858 --> 00:03:27.558
that names both.

00:03:28.052 --> 00:03:30.058
It lasts an hour, and while signed in

00:03:30.186 --> 00:03:32.106
they can never approve that merchant's change.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:36.262
And payments, orders and webhooks now show

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:37.329
every merchant together,

00:03:37.756 --> 00:03:39.334
with a merchant column and a filter.

00:03:41.326 --> 00:03:43.246
Proposed next, and not merged yet:

00:03:43.672 --> 00:03:45.550
saved cards and subscription payments,

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.451
and one billing address form for every country.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.366
That is the orchestrator,

00:03:51.708 --> 00:03:52.860
to the twenty-fifth of November:

00:03:53.244 --> 00:03:55.121
a new look proposed for the portal,

00:03:55.462 --> 00:03:57.937
an easier payment form, every processor's

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.283
answer kept, a second admin on Live

00:04:00.369 --> 00:04:03.628
changes, and one view across every merchant.

